From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:42:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] context: do not enter DMABUF mode for a probe-only
 backing

The first surface decoded into fixes the CAPTURE queue memory type:
DMABUF when that surface already has standalone backing, because a
client exported it before its first decode, MMAP otherwise.

FFmpeg gives one pool surface standalone backing without exporting it.
When it creates the frames context it derives an image of the first
surface to probe whether vaDeriveImage() works, destroys the image, and
returns the surface to its pool, from which the decoder takes it first.
Every FFmpeg VA-API decode therefore runs the queue in DMABUF mode and
prints "surface ... was exported before its first decode". Rebinding a
busy surface to an idle buffer (V4L2R_REBIND) only works on decoder
allocated MMAP buffers, so it never engages under FFmpeg.

Remember which surfaces vaExportSurfaceHandle() handed out. With
V4L2R_REBIND set, drop standalone backing that was never exported and
has no live derived image before the first decode into the surface; the
decode replaces its contents anyway. Clients that do export before
decoding keep DMABUF mode. V4L2R_REBIND=0 keeps the old behaviour.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/context.c      | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 src/surface.c      |  2 ++
 src/v4l2_request.h |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/context.c b/src/context.c
index 73e5e75..b5156ee 100644
--- a/src/context.c
+++ b/src/context.c
@@ -840,6 +840,23 @@ static int capture_buffer_bind(struct v4l2r_context *ctx,
 	 * The format converter chain has its own backing rules, keep MMAP
 	 * there.
 	 */
+	/*
+	 * Standalone backing that no client holds is not an export.
+	 * FFmpeg derives an image of one pool surface to probe whether
+	 * vaDeriveImage() works and destroys it at once; that surface is
+	 * then the first one decoded into, and its leftover backing would
+	 * put the whole queue in DMABUF mode, where busy surfaces cannot
+	 * be rebound. With V4L2R_REBIND set, drop such backing before the
+	 * first decode: the decoder output replaces its contents anyway.
+	 */
+	if (ctx->rebind_spare && !ctx->conv && index < 0 &&
+	    surface->backing && !surface->client_exported &&
+	    !surface->image_refs) {
+		v4l2r_trace("drop unexported backing of surface 0x%08x\n",
+			    surface->id);
+		v4l2r_surface_free_backing(surface);
+	}
+
 	if (!ctx->capture_memory) {
 		if (!ctx->conv && surface->backing) {
 			ctx->capture_memory = V4L2_MEMORY_DMABUF;
diff --git a/src/surface.c b/src/surface.c
index dfeafd9..12118e9 100644
--- a/src/surface.c
+++ b/src/surface.c
@@ -1073,6 +1073,8 @@ VAStatus v4l2r_ExportSurfaceHandle(VADriverContextP va_ctx, VASurfaceID surface_
 	if (status != VA_STATUS_SUCCESS)
 		return status;
 
+	surface->client_exported = true;
+
 	return fill_prime_descriptor(&view, flags, descriptor);
 }
 
diff --git a/src/v4l2_request.h b/src/v4l2_request.h
index d286e3b..c301198 100644
--- a/src/v4l2_request.h
+++ b/src/v4l2_request.h
@@ -299,6 +299,8 @@ struct v4l2r_surface {
 	VAStatus decode_status;
 	/* Derived images pin their source surface; protected by drv->mutex. */
 	unsigned int image_refs;
+	/* Handed to a client by vaExportSurfaceHandle(). */
+	bool client_exported;
 	struct v4l2r_surface_backing *backing;
 	/* A finished decode still needs (or is undergoing) format conversion
 	 * into the backing. Protected by ctx->mutex. */
